      {
        "author_name": "Fran P",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118306712302731070302/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ8kY9NN6PeLp1nu-iAMQorlXldu99JOuXWG5OtBYyC5bWgbw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "7 years ago",
        "text": "I purchased these cabinets (white MDF) via Reno Depot in 2011. By 2015 most of the doors were already chipping paint (exposing the MDF underneath)  and when I called the company to honour the 5 year warranty they claimed that it was due to excessive wear (this claim was made on the phone even before seeing the doors). I was a single person using this kitchen and used it quite minimally - I can guarantee I was not using it excessively. After coming in they refused to honour the warranty - saying that it was due to water leaking in (eg near the sink or dishwasher). Cabinet doors should be resistant to this kind of normal wear and tear. People use their sinks and dishwashers. Now I have to get the doors completely replaced as they have ALL chipped and look terrible. Would not recommend. Cabinet doors should last more than 4 years.",
        "time": 1534333076,
        "translated": false
      },
